From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoinMarket NG <dev@joinmarket-ng.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(channelescrowrpc): require an enrolled authorizer
 per signature

The escrow macaroon alone could cosign any parent that spends a channel's
funding output, so whoever held it together with the channel peer could
take the local balance. A channel must now be enrolled with a BIP340
authorizer key (AuthorizeChannel, offchain:write, outside the escrow
macaroon) before it can be frozen, and every SignParent needs that key's
signature over a tagged digest of the network, node, channel, session,
exact parent bytes, ordered spent outputs and input index.

Escrow records are written as version 2 with the policy that admitted the
partial; version 1 records still decode as policy 0 and never grant a
signature by themselves. Status and finalization of already signed
sessions are unchanged. The authorizer cannot change while an escrow
record exists, except for the first enrollment of a legacy session.
